question: >
  On runtime dependence — whether an artifact can be read and checked with
  nothing installed, or requires a particular parser, runtime, host or vendor —
  the records assert both tool and vendor binding (9 judgments, 0 authored) and
  zero dependency portability (13 judgments, 11 authored). Which should be the
  stated rule, and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

